This directory holds the Magenta-format sample sets the browser apps play
through. It is expected to exist; its contents are not tracked.

Both static folders reach it by a symlink, the way they reach the fonts:

  examples/browser/web-app/static/magenta-sound-font  →  here
  dev-tools/web-app/static/magenta-sound-font         →  here

so a set rendered once is played by every app, and `npm run setup:symlinks`
is all that connects them.

Expected layout, one directory per soundbank:

  <soundbank>/<instrument>/instrument.json
  <soundbank>/<instrument>/p<pitch>_v<velocity>.mp3

Not tracked because a full 128-instrument set is ~5,100 files and ~184 MB, and
it can be rebuilt at any time.

To regenerate (needs fluidsynth and lame on PATH — `brew install fluidsynth
lame` on macOS), from the repository root:

  node tools/magenta/generate-magenta-sound-font.js \
    examples/browser/web-app/static/sf/SGM.sf2

That writes SGM/ here. Pass an instruments range to build a subset, e.g.
'0-10,15,20,30-40' — a full set takes a long time to render.

The dev tools do the same thing through a page: "Magenta Sound Font Generator"
takes the .sf2 and writes the set here.
